Requirements: 21   with obligations: 14   deliberately none: 7

[task-01] Requirement decomposition must preserve two distinctions when it reads a task
    file: an acceptance criterion demanding a test, against the behaviour that test is
    about; and a scope exclusion, against work the change must do.
    -> preserve-test-vs-behavior-distinction  [functional/explicit]
       Requirement decomposition preserves the distinction between an acceptance
       criterion demanding a test and the behaviour that test is about.
    -> preserve-scope-exclusion-vs-work-distinction  [functional/explicit]
       Requirement decomposition preserves the distinction between a scope exclusion and
       work the change must do.

[constraint-01] An acceptance criterion that demands a test yields an obligation whose
    demand is the test, not the behaviour the test is about.
    -> acceptance-criterion-test-demand-becomes-test-obligation  [functional/explicit]
       An acceptance criterion that demands a test yields an obligation whose demand is
       the test, not the behaviour the test is about.

[constraint-02] An obligation demanding a behaviour and an obligation demanding a test
    of that behaviour are never recognised as stating the same requirement.
    -> test-behaviour-vs-test-obligation-distinct  [regression/explicit]   (also serves completion-03)
       A test asserts that an obligation demanding a behaviour and an obligation
       demanding a test of that behaviour are not recognised as stating the same
       requirement.

[constraint-03] A sentence of a given shape yields the same kind of obligation
    regardless of which task file it appears in.
    -> same-obligation-kind-across-task-files  [invariant/explicit]
       A sentence of a given shape yields the same kind of obligation regardless of
       which task file it appears in.

[constraint-04] Sibling bullets under one scope exclusions heading receive the same
    disposition as each other.
    -> sibling-scope-exclusions-same-disposition  [invariant/explicit]
       Sibling bullets under one scope exclusions heading receive the same disposition
       as each other.

[constraint-05] A requirement disposed of without an obligation carries a reason that
    does not itself state a property the change must preserve.
    -> test-no-preserve-property-reason  [regression/explicit]   (also serves completion-05)
       A test asserts that a requirement disposed of without an obligation has a reason
       stating no property the change must preserve.

[constraint-06] No obligation is produced whose only satisfying evidence would be a test
    that an excluded thing did not happen.
    -> no-test-only-evidence-for-excluded-nonoccurrence  [invariant/explicit]
       No obligation is produced whose only satisfying evidence would be a test that an
       excluded thing did not happen.

[constraint-07] Two runs over byte-identical task text produce byte-identical review
    state.
    -> test-byte-identical-review-state  [regression/explicit]   (also serves completion-06)
       A test asserts that two runs over byte-identical task text produce byte-identical
       review state.

[constraint-08] Tests issue no live model calls.
    -> tests-no-live-model-calls  [functional/explicit]
       Tests issue no live model calls.

